# Build Environment

- Before running `cmake --build`, `ninja`, or direct `cl.exe` commands on Windows, make sure the shell has Visual Studio/VC environment variables loaded. Missing VC env vars commonly show up as failures to include standard headers such as `cmath` or `float.h`.
- Prefer launching builds from a Developer PowerShell/Command Prompt, or initialize the current shell with the appropriate Visual Studio environment script before building.
- On this Windows setup, prefer `C:\Program Files\Microsoft Visual Studio\18\Community\Common7\Tools\VsDevCmd.bat` with `-arch=x64 -host_arch=x64 -vcvars_ver=14.51` when initializing the VC environment before builds, so `cl.exe` and the MSVC STL include directory come from the same toolset.
